<title>USA: Tandycrafts Q3 March 31 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Tandycrafts Q3 March 31 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>TANDYCRAFTS INC</p>
<p>				 3 Mos ended 3/31     9 Mos ended 3/31</p>
<p>					 1997   1996     1997	1996</p>
<p> Net sales		     $54,456 $53,556 $185,472  $190,252</p>
<p>Operating costs and expenses:</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold	   41,128  32,834  123,548   119,532</p>
<p> SG&amp;A			     20,062  18,186   59,499    62,362</p>
<p> Restructuring charge	     --   (501)	 --    18,317</p>
<p> Depreciation &amp; amortization 1,315   1,482    4,078     4,722</p>
<p>Total operating costs</p>
<p>  and expenses		  62,505  52,001  187,125   204,933</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)   (8,049)   1,555  (1,653)  (14,681)</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	   720     996    2,375     3,198</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>  income taxes		 (8,769)     559  (4,028)  (17,879)</p>
<p> Prov for income taxes     (3,068)     195  (1,409)   (5,873)</p>
<p> Net income		    (5,701)     364  (2,619)  (12,006)</p>
<p> Net income per share	 (0.45)    0.03   (O.21)    (1.01)</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs		  12,565  12,109   12,369    11,937</p>
<p>		    (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1997 includes $5.3 million of pretax charges to reposition Joshua's Christian Stores chain.  Charges include markdowns resulting from the liquidation of discontinued merchandise and certain costs associated with the closing of 13 under-performing stores.  Additional one-time severance expenses were also incurred as a result of personnel reductions.</p>
<p>Sales for Q3 1997 quarter were $54,456,000, up 13.5 percent compared to the same quarter last year, excluding divested operations.</p>
<p>Q3 1997 retail sales up 5.6 percent while manufacturing sales increased 24.8%.</p>
<p>Same-store sales fell 6.8 percent at Tandy Leather, while its Sav-On Office Supplies and Joshua's Christian Stores chains achieved same-store sales gains of 19.7% and 15.1%, respectively, for the quarter.</p>
<p>At manufacturing, the Frames and Framed Art division achieved a sales increase of 30.7% while TWI achieved a 14.1% sales increase.</p>
